  <static seed="19">
    <statement><p>Find the derivative of <m>1-e^{-n(e^{ax}-1)}\text{,}</m> where <m>a</m> and <m>n</m> are positive constants.</p>
<p><m>f'(x)=</m> <fillin characters="50" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>na\exp\mathopen{}\left(ax\right)\exp\mathopen{}\left(-n\mathopen{}\left(\exp\mathopen{}\left(ax\right)-1\right)\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>Using the chain rule,</p>
<p><me>\begin{aligned}
          \frac{d}{dx}\left(1-e^{-n(e^{ax}-1)}\right)
          \amp = -e^{-n(e^{ax}-1)}\left(-n ae^{ax}\right)\\
          \amp = nae^{ax}e^{-n(e^{ax}-1)}.
          \end{aligned}</me></p>
</solution>
